---
/**
 * Two-column section — columns set against each other, no surface.
 *
 * The one band on the page with no container of its own: no pane, no card, no
 * ground, not even a cut between the columns. The columns are aligned at the
 * top and opened by a rule that runs across the whole section, so they answer
 * each other point for point rather than reading as a sequence.
 *
 * This is the grid and nothing else. The columns are <SectionColumn>, written
 * as children in reading order, and their prose is Markdown in their own
 * slots — the section never sees it.
 *
 * Styling is in `src/styles/theme.css` under `.pi-twocol*`.
 *
 * ```mdx
 * <TwoColumnSection>
 *   <SectionColumn label="The usual way" title="The prompt is thrown away." recessed>
 *     Prose, as ordinary Markdown.
 *   </SectionColumn>
 *
 *   <SectionColumn label="The Piton way" title="The spec is the record.">
 *     Prose, as ordinary Markdown.
 *   </SectionColumn>
 * </TwoColumnSection>
 * ```
 */
---

<div class="pi-twocol not-content">
	<div class="pi-twocol__grid"><slot /></div>
</div>
